    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It looks like log centroid size has a significant effect on shape for my species-level dataset (output below). I&#39;m wondering if I should take this allometric effect into account when I study shape evolution in a phylogenetic context. I plan to use the PC scores as my characters for downstream comparative methods. Should I just press on regardless and use the Procrustes fit shape coordinates for PCA and then use the PC scores as my unit of analysis, or should I use the residuals from the linear model below? My apologies if this is discussed elsewhere in the forum.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Nick<br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>procD</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">f1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> two</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coords</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">999</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> I </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sequential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sums</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> of </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Squares</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Cross</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">products<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Randomized</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Residual</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Permutation</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Procedure</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Used</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Permutations</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ANOVA effect sizes </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> P</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">values based on empirical F distributions<br><br><br>           </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Df</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     SS       MS     </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rsq</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     F      Z </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Pr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0627</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.062681</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00913</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.931</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.6063</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.045</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Residuals</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">318</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.8007</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.021386</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.99087</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                      <br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Total</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">319</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6.8633</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                                       </span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><br></div>"
