     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Nick,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">The answer here is ‘it depends.’ If by downstream phylogenetic comparative methods (PCM) you mean multivariate PGLS - as found in say, ‘procD.pgls’ in geomorph\r\n or the ‘lm.rrpp’ function in RRPP (implemented as GLS) – then one may simply consider including size as an additional covariate. There is no restriction on that.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">On the other hand, if you meant some other multivariate PCM, such as evaluating phylogenetic signal or evolutionary rates, that would require a bit more thought\r\n on your system, and what aspects of trait variation you wish to capture in your analysis.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Director of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><a href=\"https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485132394000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iipUCVFEu1H7RCicfOwIz\">https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Nick<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, February 1, 2019 3:10 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] accounting for evolutionary allometry in shape evolution study<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It looks like log centroid size has a significant effect on shape for my species-level dataset (output below). I&#39;m wondering if I should take this allometric effect into account when I study shape evolution in a phylogenetic context. I\r\n plan to use the PC scores as my characters for downstream comparative methods. Should I just press on regardless and use the Procrustes fit shape coordinates for PCA and then use the PC scores as my unit of analysis, or should I use the residuals from the\r\n linear model below? My apologies if this is discussed elsewhere in the forum.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nick<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"border:solid #bbbbbb 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#fafafa\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<span>procD</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">lm</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">f1\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> two</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">d</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">array</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">coords</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">~</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> log</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">CS</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">),</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">\r\n iter </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#006666\">999</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n</span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">Type</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> I\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">Sequential</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">Sums</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> of\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#660066\">Squares</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">\r\n</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#000088\">and</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:b